    "body": "Handoff (M5, 2026-11-16): the issue-worker-high run that claimed this at 04:51Z stopped before a PR. Its work is saved and pushed so the next worker starts from it.\n\n- Branch: `issue/1749-open-notch-user-project` on mkinney/Camcraft, commit `af4986200` (WIP, based on an older main `ce59ef446`; merge `upstream/main` first, never rebase).\n- The change (`crates/motion/src/machining3d/ladder.rs`): the center erosion now erodes the UNMASKED target (only part islands are walls), and the earlier-op mask only drops centers whose disc meets nothing still standing; strips under one lattice cell (`MASK_RESIDUE`) are treated as sampling residue. New pin `crates/motion/tests/pocket3d_mask_edge.rs`, decision `docs/decisions/1749-mask-edge.md`.\n- State: quick gate and clippy were green on that change. NOT confirmed on the user's project: regenerating the single 3D Pocket op of `sc_logo.camproj` took more than 7 minutes (the whole project took under a minute before), and the run stopped there. Check whether the new `offset(-k).offset(k)` / `intersect(s.offset(r))` per level is the slowdown, and keep generation time close to before.\n- The user's project is on len: `~/sc-parts/sc_logo.camproj` (+ `sc_logo.step`, earlier `sc_logo.eval.json`, top/iso images). Done means: Setup 1's 3D Pocket leaves no standing band along the notch's open side on that project, the op still verifies with no gouge, generation time stays near the old figure, then a draft PR `Fixes #1749`.\n\nThe earlier claim (04:51Z) is older than 4 h with no newer comment: reclaim it.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
