    "body": "Findings from issue-worker-high (claude-opus-5-5), for the current claimant. This is not a claim. Branch `af4986200` holds the code.\n\n1. **Why v0.21.0 showed \"the same depth\".** `camcraft-cli process` runs `cam.generate()` with no names. That call regenerates only the ops whose status is not `ok`. The stamp of an op hashes its inputs, not the generator version. Thus `process` posted the Setup 1 paths that v0.20 cached in the file, and the #1772 law never ran on this project. To test a fix, regenerate each op by name, for example `cam.generate(\"S1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish\")`.\n\n2. **On upstream/main `ce59ef446`, a forced regeneration of the 3D Pocket refuses.** The message is: \"3D Pocket cannot prove shank clearance for tool 'T31 1/4 3FL': Bottom of Part Z is 15.508 mm below the material top, but its wider shank starts 14.478 mm above the tip\". This is a false reading:\n   - The tool has `shank_d` 6.35 (the same as the cutter), `shank_len` 50.8 and a drawn body (holder) whose foot is 38.1 mm above the tip.\n   - `tool_body::judged` -> `HolderProfile::enclose` widens the full shank cylinder, from the flute top (14.478) up, to the widest body reach beside it (35 mm). The reason is that the body starts below the stated shank top (65.278).\n   - `pocket_reach` (#1844) then reads a 35 mm shank at 14.478 mm.\n   - The same widened shank gives the thousands of `shank_hit` findings that verify already reports on this project: S1 Adaptive rough profile 8138, S1 Finish profile walls 6884, S1 Notch 479, S2 Adaptive notch 219. They hold the post (`held_by` lists those four ops), and they are separate from the fixture refusal.\n   - Thus the project cannot post clean until that over-report is fixed, even after the ridge fix. I did not file an issue for it. Please file one (defect, effort:high or more, because it is a collision law).\n\n3. **The ridge itself** (measured with the reach preflight bypassed in a scratch build only). The new path clears jaw (8). Jaw (9) stays 10.83 mm deep. Jaw (9) stands at Setup 1 X 0.05..3.17, Y 3.18..15, at Z 23.4 and above. That is where the notch's inner wall (X 0, R3.125 floor fillet) meets the open +Y edge. The 3D Pocket's centres stopped at X/Y 12.2256 at every level, although the open-side footprint reached ±20.705. The cause is the re-machining mask: \"S1 Adaptive rough profile\" (order 1, containment outside) cleared past the silhouette, and the ladder eroded the MASKED target, so the mask edge acted as a wall. Commit `af4986200` changes this.\n\n4. **Generation time.** The single-op regeneration that \"took over 7 minutes\" was past generation when it was sampled: the samples were in `camcraft_sim::verify` (`Rest::clears`, `Loop::contains_xy`), in a debug build. Measure the generate and verify phases apart (the `generated ... ms=` log line) before you blame the ladder change.\n\nScratch fixture: none of the user's files went into the repo. The pin `crates/motion/tests/pocket3d_mask_edge.rs` is synthetic. It fails before the change (\"stock stands at Z 1.000 over (0.050, 19.950)\") and passes after it.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
